---
// Editorial intro block for the homepage.
// Positioned between hero and tool grid.
// Purpose: signal to Google (and visitors) that this is an editorial listicle
// with opinions, methodology, and structure — not just a logo wall.
//
// SEO targets: "media planning tools", "media planning tool", "best media planning tools",
// "media planning software". Uses H2 structure for clear topical relevance.
---

<section class="homepage-editorial mt-4 mb-10">
  <div class="prose prose-gray dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
    <p class="lead text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      We track <strong>50+ media planning tools</strong> — from free omnichannel planners to
      $250K/year enterprise suites. This page ranks the platforms worth a serious look in 2026,
      with transparent pricing, real channel coverage, and honest notes on who each tool is (and
      isn't) for.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50 mt-8 mb-4">
      Our top picks at a glance
    </h2>
    <div class="not-prose grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-2 mb-6">
      <a href="/halliard" class="block p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 hover:border-primary-300 dark:hover:border-primary-700 hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-750 transition-colors">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 dark:bg-emerald-900/30 dark:text-emerald-400 mb-2">Best free</span>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Halliard</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Free omnichannel R&amp;F planning across 18+ channels. No credit card.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/basis" class="block p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 hover:border-primary-300 dark:hover:border-primary-700 hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-750 transition-colors">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium bg-primary-100 text-primary-700 dark:bg-primary-900/30 dark:text-primary-400 mb-2">Best for agencies</span>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Basis</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">#1-rated on G2 (4.5/5, 287+ reviews). Plan + buy across channels in one suite.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/nielsen-media-impact" class="block p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 hover:border-primary-300 dark:hover:border-primary-700 hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-750 transition-colors">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium bg-violet-100 text-violet-700 dark:bg-violet-900/30 dark:text-violet-400 mb-2">Best for TV / cross-media R&amp;F</span>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Nielsen Media Impact</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">MRC-accredited audience data. The standard for TV-led planners.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/bionic" class="block p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 hover:border-primary-300 dark:hover:border-primary-700 hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-750 transition-colors">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 dark:bg-amber-900/30 dark:text-amber-400 mb-2">Best mid-market</span>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Bionic</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Transparent pricing from $199/user/mo. 14-day trial. Built for indie agencies.</p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50 mt-8 mb-4">
      How we rank media planning tools
    </h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
      We evaluate every platform on five criteria: <strong>channel coverage</strong> (how many
      paid channels it plans across — programmatic, CTV, linear TV, paid social, search, audio,
      OOH), <strong>pricing transparency</strong> (is there a public rate card?),
      <strong>reach &amp; frequency modeling</strong> (accurate audience overlap math, or just
      spreadsheet math?), <strong>collaboration</strong> (versioning, multi-user, agency-to-client
      handoff), and <strong>fit</strong> (who the tool is actually built for — solo planners,
      mid-market agencies, or enterprise networks). We don't take payment from vendors for
      placement.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50 mt-8 mb-4">
      Who this directory is for
    </h2>
    <ul class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
      <li><strong>Media planners</strong> at agencies and brands choosing or upgrading their planning stack.</li>
      <li><strong>Agency leads</strong> evaluating end-to-end suites (Mediaocean, Basis, Strata) vs. best-of-breed combos.</li>
      <li><strong>CMOs and VPs of Media</strong> comparing enterprise tools before a procurement cycle.</li>
      <li><strong>Solo planners and freelancers</strong> looking for free or low-cost tools that don't sacrifice channel breadth.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-6 italic">
      Disclosure: Halliard, which sponsors this directory, is listed as the "Best free" pick.
      Every other entry below is editorially ranked — no paid placements.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
